From: Tetris port maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] regulator: mt6315: preserve mode read failures before writes

The MT6319-compatible provider supplies both camera VMM and GPU VGPU.
Do not change either rail's mode after a failed current-mode read. A request
for the already selected normal mode is a successful no-op, not EINVAL.
No provider, consumer or power-producing DT node is enabled here.

diff --git a/drivers/regulator/mt6315-regulator.c b/drivers/regulator/mt6315-regulator.c
--- a/drivers/regulator/mt6315-regulator.c
+++ b/drivers/regulator/mt6315-regulator.c
@@ -123,6 +123,8 @@ static int mt6315_regulator_set_mode(struct regulator_dev *rdev,
 	info = container_of(rdev->desc, struct mt6315_regulator_info, desc);
 	modeset_mask = init->modeset_mask[rdev_get_id(rdev)];
 	curr_mode = mt6315_regulator_get_mode(rdev);
+	if (curr_mode < 0)
+		return curr_mode;
 	switch (mode) {
 	case REGULATOR_MODE_FAST:
 		ret = regmap_update_bits(rdev->regmap,
@@ -147,6 +149,8 @@ static int mt6315_regulator_set_mode(struct regulator_dev *rdev,
 						 info->lp_mode_mask,
 						 0);
 			usleep_range(100, 110);
+		} else if (curr_mode == REGULATOR_MODE_NORMAL) {
+			ret = 0;
 		} else {
 			ret = -EINVAL;
 		}
